    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d11">

                <pb facs="0026" n="14" sameAs="frus:frus1943v02/pg14"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">859.00/1083</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Secretary of State to President
                        Roosevelt </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-09-15">September 15,
                        1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Memorandum to the President</hi>
                </p>
                <p>I understand that on September 4, 1943 the Danish Minister presented to you a
                    request for the issuance by you and Mr. Churchill of a statement regarding
                    recent events in Denmark.<anchor n="17" xml:id="d11-f1"/> Subsequently he <pb
                        facs="0027" n="15" xml:id="pg15"/> spoke to me about this matter and also
                    gave me a copy of a draft statement<anchor n="18" xml:id="d11-f2"/> which he had
                    prepared.</p>
                <p>I believe that on balance a statement of this sort should be issued. There is
                    evidence to indicate that the Germans now realize that it was a mistake to force
                    the resignation of the Government in Copenhagen. Recent press reports indicate
                    that they have approached several political leaders in connection with the
                    possible formation of a new government. A statement by you and, if possible, by
                    you and Mr. Churchill would do much to deter the Danes from any form of future
                    collaboration with Germany and would encourage the Danish people in their
                    resistance to German rule.</p>
                <p>A redraft<anchor n="19" xml:id="d11-f3"/> of the Minister’s statement is attached
                    for your consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>C[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ordell</hi>] H[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >ull</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d11-f1" n="17" xml:id="d11-f1-content">
                <p>After the resignation of the Danish Government on August 28, 1943, German troops
                    entered Copenhagen and took over the most important administrative posts of the
                    city. In a number of places there were incidents of conflict between Danes and
                    Germans and a state of emergency was declared.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d11-f2" n="18" xml:id="d11-f2-content">
                <p>See draft statement, <ref target="#pg12">p. 12</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d11-f3" n="19" xml:id="d11-f3-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
